#!/usr/bin/env npc
jinx_name: fix_hn_header_agent_2026_09
description: |
  Dated agent-style fix jinx for September 2026.
  Invokes the renderer NPC as an agent to fix the Hacker News header
  logo/upvote/text-weight differences. The agent uses the renderer's own
  jinxes (load_file, edit_file, cargo_check, render_compare) and reports back.
inputs:
  - url: "https://news.ycombinator.com"
  - name: "hn"

steps:
  - name: dispatch_renderer
    engine: agent
    query: |
      Fix the Hacker News header rendering in Incognidium.

      The render of https://news.ycombinator.com (use render_compare jinx with name "hn")
      shows these defects compared to Firefox:
      1. Missing white logo box behind the orange YC glyph in the top header.
      2. Upvote triangles are solid filled instead of hollow/outline.
      3. Body text is lighter/thinner than Firefox.

      Repository: /home/caug/incognidium
      Important rules:
      - Read relevant source files first with load_file.
      - Make surgical Rust edits with edit_file.
      - Run cargo_check after every edit.
      - Use render_compare to verify each attempt.
      - Do not modify render_to_png.rs; it is only a viewport wrapper.
      - Stop after 3 failed hypotheses or when the render improves.

      Return a brief report: what you changed, why, and whether the render improved.
